---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: literature.html
navKey: literature
section: literature
crumb: Literature
title: Literature
nextHref: models.html
nextLabel: Models & Data
description: Key papers, tagged by subtype and by how they connect to machine learning.
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/lit-graph.js
  - /assets/js/paper-table.js
---
<script>window.PAPERS = {{ papers | dump | safe }};</script>

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="supergraphic">{{ site.stats.papers }}</div>
  <div class="eyebrow rise rise-1">{{ site.stats.papers }} papers</div>
  <h1 class="rise rise-2">The <em>literature</em>.</h1>
  <p class="lede rise rise-3">Key papers, tagged by subtype and by how they connect to machine learning — kept as a working reference, not a static bibliography.</p>
</header>

<section class="rise rise-4">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="section-title">Paper network</div>
    <div class="section-note mono">drag nodes · hover for details</div>
  </div>
  <div id="lit-graph-container">
    <canvas id="lit-graph-canvas"></canvas>
    <div class="graph-tooltip" id="graph-tooltip"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="graph-note">Node size reflects tag count. Lines connect papers sharing tags. Thickness = shared tags.</p>
</section>

<section class="rise rise-5">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="section-title">All papers</div>
    <div class="section-note mono" id="paper-count"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="paper-table-wrap">
    <table class="paper-table" id="paper-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th data-col="title" class="sortable">Title <span class="sort-arr">↕</span></th>
          <th data-col="author" class="sortable">Author <span class="sort-arr">↕</span></th>
          <th data-col="year" class="sortable">Year <span class="sort-arr">↓</span></th>
          <th data-col="topic" class="sortable">Topic <span class="sort-arr">↕</span></th>
          <th data-col="journal" class="sortable">Journal <span class="sort-arr">↕</span></th>
          <th data-col="country" class="sortable">Country <span class="sort-arr">↕</span></th>
          <th data-col="tags">Tags</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="paper-tbody"></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>
